      "message": "Oh, thanks for sharing. But here it\u0027s becoming complicated because nodeid \u003d\u003d 0 is the valid case, so I don\u0027t want to do something like this:\n```\n(fii-\u003ebacking_inode !\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 fii-\u003ebacking_inode \u003d\u003d fi-\u003ebacking_inode) \u0026\u0026\n    (fii-\u003enodeid !\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 fii-\u003enodeid \u003d\u003d fi-\u003enodeid)\n```\n\nWhat do you think about this one? With this approach we will cover case you mentioned above, but only if nodeid !\u003d 0:\n\n```\n#ifdef CONFIG_FUSE_BPF\n\tif (fii-\u003ebacking_inode) {\n\t\treturn fii-\u003ebacking_inode \u003d\u003d fi-\u003ebacking_inode \u0026\u0026\n\t\t    (fii-\u003enodeid !\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 fii-\u003enodeid \u003d\u003d fi-\u003enodeid);\n\t}\n#endif\n        return fii-\u003enodeid \u003d\u003d fi-\u003enodeid;\n```\n\nDo you have any better options?",
