      "message": "But seams like case you mentioned isn\u0027t supported by https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android13-5.10:common/fs/fuse/inode.c;l\u003d356-388 anyway.\n\nSo basically we currently have 2 different ways to get the inode:\n\n1. Based on their nodeid: https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android13-5.10:common/fs/fuse/inode.c;l\u003d390-446\n2. Based on their backing_inode: https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android13-5.10:common/fs/fuse/inode.c;l\u003d356-388 anyway.\n\nSo, for case you mentioned above we just need to use the first one or just introduce the third option which will consider both. \n\nBut I think it should be out of the context for this change.",
